# PMSM RL Project Rules

## Project goal
Build a Python simulation project for reinforcement learning current control of a PMSM.
Use gym-electric-motor as the physical environment layer when possible.
Focus on modular, readable, research-friendly code.

## Code style
- Use Python 3.10+
- Prefer small modules with clear responsibilities
- Add docstrings to public classes and functions
- Use type hints when practical
- Avoid giant single-file implementations
- Keep training, evaluation, plotting, and environment construction separated

## Project architecture
- envs/: GEM environment creation and wrappers
- agents/: RL algorithms and neural networks
- baselines/: PI current controller baseline
- configs/: experiment and environment configs
- utils/: logging, checkpointing, metrics
- outputs/: generated results only

## Engineering constraints
- Do not invent unavailable APIs
- If gym-electric-motor API is uncertain, first inspect installed package or current codebase
- Always explain which files will be created or modified before large edits
- Prefer incremental implementation over full rewrite
- After editing, suggest terminal commands to test the changed code

## Research constraints
- The first target is single PMSM current control in Python simulation
- Start with a minimal runnable version
- Prioritize current tracking, limit handling, logging, and reproducibility